[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5072558674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121723#issuecomment-5072558674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121723","id":5072558674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLlkaUg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T17:18:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T17:18:47Z","body":"I'm a little skeptical about these changes. The original bug was reported against 4.0, but you are suggesting that the offending code was introduced in 4.3. I suspect there is something else at play here and you have randomly stumbled on a workaround that isn't a proper fix. \r\n\r\nTreating reverse-z values as non-reverse-z doesn't logically make sense. Which makes me think that there real issue is elsewhere. Most likely there is some other parameter that needs to be changed. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5072558674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073051838","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121723#issuecomment-5073051838","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121723","id":5073051838,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLmCgvg","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T18:15:04Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T18:15:04Z","body":"I believe I know what's going on. The Penumbra sign was flipped by this, which flips the sample scale direction.\r\n\r\nMy hunch is currently the penumbra scale would in the \"should be dark areas\" scale the samples towards nonblocked areas thus lightening them, but in the \"should be lighter areas\" the scale makes it sample more towards the blocked areas thus darkening them, when the opposite is desired for the proper result.\r\n\r\nIf I'm right, a simple negative sign on penumbra would likely result in the same result","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073051838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084813014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121723#issuecomment-5084813014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121723","id":5084813014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLxQW1g","user":{"login":"mrcdk","id":483531,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzUzMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/483531?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk","html_url":"https://github.com/mrcdk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T18:27:30Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T18:27:30Z","body":"After some shader debugging with renderdoc I noticed the following. What I don't know is if `penumbra` has an specific range like `(0, 1)` or not. It'll be easier to explain with an example.\r\n\r\nLet's say we are trying to get the `penumbra` for `depth = 0.3`. We search for the blockers and we find one blocker with depth `0.8` so we end with `blocker_avg = 0.8 / blocker_count = 0.8 / 1.0 = 0.8` :\r\n\r\nOld formula: `penumbra = (-depth + blocker_avg) / (1.0 - blocker_avg) = (-03 + 0.8) / (1.0 - 0.8) = 2.5` The value goes outside the `penumbra` range I assumed but maybe I'm wrong about this assumption and the `penumbra` can go outside that range. I've not able to find a clear answer anywhere.\r\n\r\nNew formula: `penumbra = (depth - blocker_avg) / blocker_avg = (0.3 - 0.8) / 0.8 = -0.625` Value is negative, maybe I should  swap the subtraction but let's continue.\r\n\r\nNow let's try a more extreme example: `depth = 0.001` and `blocker_avg = 0.998`\r\n\r\nOld formula: `penumbra = (-0.001 + 0.998) / (1.0 - 0.998) = 498.5` This is a huge value and I don't think this is correct, is it?\r\n\r\nNew formula: `penumbra = (0.001 - 0.998) / 0.998 = -0.999` It's still negative but whatever, it's inside the range I assumed.\r\n\r\nI also tried clamping the old formula from 0.0 to 1.0\r\n\r\n| type | master | clamp | PR |\r\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|\r\n| omni (size 0.5m) |  <img width=\"1345\" height=\"824\" alt=\"master-omni\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df679b9b-51ac-4ded-bb36-9bb6da57f8b5\" /> | <img width=\"1345\" height=\"824\" alt=\"clamp-omni\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34688e21-d41c-4b07-8e13-49549cb7b755\" /> | <img width=\"1345\" height=\"824\" alt=\"fix-omni\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bbad7645-f0d8-45ef-849d-1253ec8c6f27\" /> |\r\n| directional 1 (angular distance 1º) | <img width=\"1249\" height=\"937\" alt=\"master-directional-1\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07e571dd-b2cd-45ab-bc86-339de8c6f02b\" /> | <img width=\"1249\" height=\"937\" alt=\"clamp-directional-1\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cae59993-645d-4e57-b116-2e9849025d65\" /> | <img width=\"1249\" height=\"937\" alt=\"fix-directional-1\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ea11a0a9-d6f7-4479-971b-bd9350b32d51\" /> |\r\n| directional 2 (angular distance 1º) | <img width=\"1780\" height=\"904\" alt=\"master-directional-2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82c11355-e646-4616-af81-3c4d7d6dfff1\" /> | <img width=\"1780\" height=\"904\" alt=\"clamp-directional-2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ab40b645-3da8-4972-a3ee-c19910f4cffa\" /> | <img width=\"1780\" height=\"904\" alt=\"fix-directional-2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/100a18f5-70cd-4441-8a94-ab9cf71c7db8\" /> | \r\n\r\nWhich one is closer to real life? 🤷\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084813014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084895735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121723#issuecomment-5084895735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121723","id":5084895735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLxVZ9w","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T18:50:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T18:50:09Z","body":"good sanity check would be to see how split transitions look between the two with directional shadows.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084895735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5087660732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121723#issuecomment-5087660732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121723","id":5087660732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLz-KvA","user":{"login":"mrcdk","id":483531,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzUzMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/483531?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk","html_url":"https://github.com/mrcdk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrcdk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T05:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T05:40:38Z","body":"Okay, screenshots without blending the splits:\r\n\r\n|  | master | clamp | PR |\r\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|\r\n| 1 normal | <img width=\"1510\" height=\"811\" alt=\"master-directional-1\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f